The '''SE-14r light repeating blaster''',<ref name="Guide" /> also known as the '''SE-14r blaster pistol''', the '''SE-14r blaster rifle''',<ref name="Imperial Troops">{{EncyclopediaCite|Imperial Troops}}</ref> or simply the '''SE-14 pistol''',<ref name="USE">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Ultimate Sticker Encyclopedia]]''</ref> was a [[light repeating blaster]] manufactured by [[BlasTech Industries]].<ref name="Guide" />

==Description==
[[File:Unlimited-WarzoneLt.png|thumb|left|330px|An Imperial officer fires their SE-14r in battle.]]
Manufactured by [[BlasTech Industries]], the SE-14r light repeating blaster was a model of a [[light repeating blaster]] in the form of a pistol. The weapon was designed to be disassembled and fitted with a [[scope]].<ref name="Guide" /> Related to the [[SE-14C blaster pistol]],<ref name="DB">{{Databank|se-14-blaster-pistol|SE-14 blaster pistol}}</ref> it was used by personnel of the [[Galactic Empire]], including the [[Imperial Intelligence]]'s [[death trooper]]s,<ref name="Guide" /> regular [[stormtrooper]]s,<ref name="SE-14r storm">{{Fathead|url=star-wars/star-wars-movies/stormtrooper-teammate-decal|text=Stormtrooper Teammate Decal}}</ref><ref name="SW (2020) 19">[[Star Wars (2020) 19|''Star Wars'' (2020) 19]]</ref> and some [[Imperial officer|officers]].<ref name="KH">{{RebelsMagCite|4|Kallus' Hunt}}</ref> At one time, it was only used by Imperial officers.<ref name="TROS VD">''[[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary]]''</ref> [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] owned [[Lando Calrissian's SE-14r light repeating blasters|two SE-14r blasters]] with one of them featuring an long barrel that also act like a noise suppressor for long-distance targets<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> and another one was used to create a [[prod pistol]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

==History==
===Imperial Era===
At some point, an [[Imperial officer]] with the [[Military rank|rank]] of [[lieutenant]] wielded a SE-14r and rushed into battle with the weapon, leading their [[swamp trooper]]s through a [[forest]].<ref name="WarzoneLt">{{SWU|set=Shadows of the Galaxy|cardname=Warzone Lieutenant|link=0336440515|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20250523133558/https://swudb.com/card/SHD/110/warzone-lieutenant}}</ref> During his time as a [[smuggler]], [[Landonis Balthazar Calrissian|Lando Calrissian]] owned [[Lando Calrissian's SE-14r light repeating blasters|two chromium-plated SE-14r]] with [[Tibrin]] [[Tibrin mother-of-pearl|mother-of-pearl]] handles and removable barrel extensions.<ref name="SoloOG">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story The Official Guide]]''</ref> He used one of the SE-14r on missions to [[Kullgroon]]<ref name="LandoDON2">[[Lando - Double or Nothing 2|''Lando - Double or Nothing'' 2]]</ref> and [[Kessel]].<ref name="Solo">''[[Solo: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref> [[Rio Durant]] carried two SE-14r blasters and fought off several [[Cloud-Riders]] on [[Vandor]], who boarded his stolen [[Y-45 armored transport hauler]] before being [[Death|fatally]] shot in the back by [[Baroosh Pawk]] but Durant managed to kill the [[pirate]].<ref name="Solo" />

[[File:TalaOpensFire-OWKpIII.png|thumb|right|270px|Imperial officer turned defector Tala Durith wielded an SE-14r.]]
In [[9 BBY]],<ref name="9 BBY">The events of ''[[Star Wars: Obi-Wan Kenobi]]'' takes place in [[9 BBY]] per the reasoning [[Template:KenobiDate|here]].</ref> Imperial officer [[Tala Durith]], secretly a defector who had been helping smuggle [[Force-sensitive]]s to safety as part of the [[Hidden Path]], wielded a SE-14r during her service within the [[Mapuzo battery|battery]] of Imperial forces stationed on the mining planet [[Mapuzo]]. During the [[Battle on Mapuzo]], Durith killed several of the [[stormtrooper]]s under her command to rescue [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and [[Princess]] [[Leia Skywalker Organa Solo|Leia Organa]] from arrest.<ref name="Part III" />

Around [[4 BBY]], [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] used an SE-14r blaster when [[Theft of the TIE Avenger prototype|stealing]] the [[TIE Avenger prototype]] from [[Sienar Test Facility 73]], using it to shoot a [[Unidentified Sienar droid|Sienar droid]]. He discarded the blaster after landing on [[Yavin 4]] and meeting the [[Maya Pei Brigade]], who assumed he was an Imperial due to his [[Sienar test pilot]] uniform.<ref>{{Andor|One Year Later}}</ref> During the [[Ghorman Massacre]], in [[2 BBY]], some members of the [[Ghorman Front]], including [[Enza Rylanz]] and [[Dreena]], wielded SE-14rs, but were ineffective against the [[Imperial security trooper]]s and the six [[KX-series security droid]]s that were deployed.<ref name="AWAY" />

In [[5 BBY]],<ref name="Kallus Hunt Date">{{EmailCite|email=Wookieepedia:Email/Martin Fisher|creator=[[Martin Fisher]]|date=2016-01-14}} states that "Kallus' Hunt" takes place between "[[Breaking Ranks]]" and "[[Out of Darkness]]." "Breaking Ranks" is dated to [[5 BBY]] by ''[[Star Wars: Galactic Atlas]]'', and "Out of Darkness" is dated to 5 [['ABY-BBY' dating system|BBY]] in {{FactFile2014|84|5 BBY 27-30|Out of Darkness}}, meaning that "Kallus' Hunt" must also take place in 5 BBY.</ref> the rogue Imperial [[lieutenant]] [[Jovan]] carried one such pistol, which he used against [[Imperial Security Bureau|ISB]] [[Agent]] [[Alexsandr Kallus|Kallus]] while trying to escape Imperial justice.<ref name="KH" /> [[K-2SO]], a reprogrammed Imperial [[security droid]], was given an SE-14r by [[Jyn Erso]] on [[Scarif]] in the [[Citadel Tower]]'s [[Scarif vault|vault]] which he used to fight off the stormtroopers.<ref name="Rogue One">''[[Rogue One: A Star Wars Story]]''</ref>

Shortly after the [[War of the Bounty Hunters]], a hooded [[Luke Skywalker]] attempted to [[mind trick]] two stormtroopers on the river [[moon]] of [[Al'doleem]] to gain information on what the Empire was doing on Al'doleem. Both troopers were armed with SE-14rs. Still dealing with the recent trauma of losing his right hand during the [[duel on Cloud City]], Skywalker's mind trick attempt, which he attempted to perform with his still-new [[Cybernetics|cybernetic]] hand, failed. Both troopers raised their SE-14s at the man they assumed to merely be an out of line civilian, ordering him to leave. Maintaining his cover, Skywalker did so and informed his [[astromech droid]], [[R2-D2]], they would need a new plan.<ref name="SW (2020) 19" />

===New Republic Era===
[[File:Manga-Mando-Stormtroopers.png|thumb|left|200px|A stormtrooper of Gideon's remnant points their SE-14r at Din Djarin]]
In [[9 ABY]],<ref name="9 ABY">{{MandoDate}}</ref> members of [[Moff]] [[Gideon]]'s [[Gideon's Imperial remnant|Imperial remnant]] utilized this weapon, including stormtroopers<ref name="Chapter 7">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 7: The Reckoning}}</ref> and [[Imperial officer]]s.<ref name="Chapter 11">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 11: The Heiress}}</ref> While undercover as a [[Juggernaut Pilot]] of the [[Morak Imperial remnants]], [[Din Djarin]] used an SE-14r to kill several [[Shydopp pirates|pirates]] attempting to destroy a stolen [[HCVw A9.2 juggernaut transport]] on [[Morak]]. The weapon either malfunctioned or ran out of charge not long afterwards, at which point Djarin hurled it ineffectually at one of his assailants and resorted to [[Unarmed combat|hand-to-hand combat]] to fend the rest of them off.<ref name="KH" />

Members of the [[Strassi family]] and [[Aqualish crime family]] of [[Mos Espa]] later used SE-14rs. However, the [[Battle of Mos Espa|showdown on Tatooine]] largely wiped their forces, cementing the [[Fett gotra]] as the leading crime family on [[Tatooine]].<ref name="Honor" /> Several [[Imperial armored commando]]s also used a [[scope]]less SE-14r while fighting [[Din Djarin]] in the [[ray shield]]s to Gideon's command center on [[Mandalore]].<ref name="Chapter 24">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 24: The Return}}</ref>

Also in 9 ABY,<ref name="Hunters Date">{{HuntersDate}}</ref> the [[KX-series security droid]] [[K-A0S]] joined the [[Hunters of the Outer Rim]] competition,<ref name="Controlled K-A0S">{{ArenaNews|url=b8323ac908e94287a94cae61bf8ee1c7-en-gb|text=Controlled K-A0S}}</ref> in which she wielded a SE-14r grafted to a small limb built into her back as a [[shoulder-mounted armament]].<ref name="Hunters" /> By [[35 ABY]], Lando Calrissian had used one of his [[chromium]] SE-14r to create a custom-crafted [[prod pistol]].<ref name="TROS VD" />

